==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la}} {{term|divisibilis|lang=la}}, from the verb {{term|divido||lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|[dɪˈvɪzɪbəɫ]}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Capable of being [[divide]]d or split.
# {{arithmetic}} Of an [[integer]], that, when [[divide]]d by another integer, leaves no [[remainder]].
#: ''12 is '''divisible''' by 3.''

